<title>USA: Ameritech seeks FCC long-distance approval.</title>
<headline>Ameritech seeks FCC long-distance approval.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ameritech Corp said Thursday it asked U.S. regulators for approval to offer long-distance phone service in Michigan, making it the first Baby Bell to seek approval to provide long-distance service in its own region.</p>
<p>Under last year's communications law, the Federal Communications Commission could permit Ameritech and other Bells to offer in-region long-distance service if the agency determined these carriers had opened their own local network to new rivals, such as long-distance companies and others.</p>
</text>
